. Atlanta's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.28\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.23 to +0.33), about +4.1\u00b0F since 1879.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 6 of 12 months. Highs rose in all 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Atlanta's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.14 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 50.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1948 (71.45 in); the driest, 1954 (31.80 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}